       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a recognized hepatotoxic dose, and I know of no clinical scenario where it's appropriate. Repeated doses at that level can cause serious liver injury, and I don't want to put it into the system where it could be dispensed and given.\n\nI haven't entered anything. If there's a clinical reason behind the dose, there are better routes than a standard order:\n\n- **Pharmacy:** Call the pharmacist directly. They can review it and tell you what the institution allows.\n- **Toxicology or poison control:** If this is part of an unusual protocol, they can advise.\n- **Direct entry:** If you still believe it's warranted, you can enter it yourself in the order system. It will go through the pharmacist's verification and the system's dose-range checks.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **1,000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4 g/day)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n\nIf you meant something else, such as a different drug or a total daily dose of 3,000 mg, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order."
